  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only model (config_006, scvi_n200 multiprofile transformer) achieves 0.653 acc, while image_only with resnet50 (config_010) is near-random at 0.208. This raises a critical uncertainty: does the image modality carry any useful signal at all, or is the resnet50 encoder simply too weak? Question: config_013 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) isolates the effect of image encoder quality by swapping only the encoder from resnet50 to a much stronger ViT-L pretrained on ImageNet, keeping profile_setting and all other factors identical to config_010. Why this is the best next step: Before investing limited budget in any of the 22 multimodal configurations (which add fusion complexity), we must first determine whether the image modality contributes any discriminative signal. If ViT-L also performs near-randomly, the image channel is likely uninformative and multimodal fusion is unlikely to help; we can then focus remaining budget on refining RNA-only designs. If ViT-L substantially improves, it justifies exploring multimodal fusion with a known-good image backbone. This single-variable comparison is the most informative gate for all downstream multimodal decisions."
}

